# overnight.env — runtime feature flags for the overnight launchers (ARCH-342).
#
# INSTALL TO:  ~/.config/convivy/overnight.env
# Both launchers (launch-overnight, launch-overnight-hollis) source that path if it
# exists. This file is the committed reference for what the flags mean; the live copy
# is machine-local, because a canary is a property of THIS machine's rollout, not of
# the code.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# These flags used to live in the launchd plists, set by hand with PlistBuddy and
# never committed. That drifted the live plists away from their repo templates, and
# `install.sh` copies templates OVER the live plists — so running the installer would
# have silently reverted the sous-chef phase-split canary and the digest assembler,
# turning fragment mode off and re-breaking the consolidated digest. Found 2026-07-13,
# before it fired. Plists now carry only program + schedule + PATH + budget caps, all
# of which match their template exactly, so there is nothing left to drift.
#
# It also kills the ARCH-104 friction: a plist env change needs bootout+bootstrap
# (kickstart -k reuses the old job definition), which is why flipping a canary was a
# launchctl ritual. A change here takes effect on the NEXT run, no launchctl at all.
#
# Every value is OPTIONAL — an absent file means "all flags off", which is the
# pre-canary default behavior. The launcher logs its active flags each night, so the
# run log always records what actually ran.

# --- Phase-split (ARCH-268) --------------------------------------------------
# Run the overnight as discrete stages (triage → fix-drain → verify → digest)
# instead of one monolithic orchestrator. 0/unset = off.
OVERNIGHT_PHASE_SPLIT=1
# Restrict phase-split to these products (space- or comma-separated). Unset = every
# product, which is NOT what you want during a canary.
#
# constance and vivy joined sous-chef on 2026-07-23 (Slack sunset Tier 1.1). The
# monolithic path they were on resolved prior approvals by reading REACTIONS in
# #<product>-proposals; the operator stopped reading Slack on 07-21, so those approvals had
# become undecidable rather than merely undecided. The phase-split triage stage
# resolves them from the decision board instead (ARCH-380). hollis and selector are
# deliberately still monolithic — hollis has its own launcher, which never reads
# this flag.
OVERNIGHT_PHASE_SPLIT_PRODUCTS=sous-chef,constance,vivy

# --- Digest fragment mode (ARCH-331 / ARCH-337 / ARCH-338) -------------------
# A product in fragment mode WRITES its digest section to a fragment file and posts
# nothing; the 06:00 overnight-digest-assemble job consolidates every fragment into
# the single #overnight-digest post. A product NOT listed here self-posts its own
# digest under its own `overnight-digest-<product>-<date>` once-key (ARCH-338).
OVERNIGHT_DIGEST_ASSEMBLER=1
# Both launchers read this same list and each checks it PER PRODUCT, so one combined
# list serves both: launch-overnight matches sous-chef, launch-overnight-hollis
# matches hollis.
OVERNIGHT_DIGEST_ASSEMBLER_PRODUCTS=sous-chef,hollis

# --- Base branch the checkout guard parks a stray checkout onto (ARCH-341) ---
# OVERNIGHT_BASE_BRANCH=main
